All 14 tests pass. Here's a summary of the changes:

**`app/auth.py`** — Implemented `require_api_key`:
- Reads `X-API-Key` header via `Header()`
- Returns 401 if the header is missing
- Returns 401 if the key is not in `VALID_API_KEYS`
- Returns the associated username on success (for potential future use)

**`app/main.py`** — All endpoint changes:

| Endpoint | Change |
|---|---|
| `GET /tasks` | Added `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` optional filters (combinable), plus `page`/`page_size` pagination with defaults of 1/20 |
| `POST /tasks` | New — requires auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`, validates `project_id` exists (404 if not), auto-generates ID, returns 201 |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | New — requires auth, partial update via `TaskUpdate` with `exclude_unset=True` so only provided fields are changed, returns 404 if not found |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | New — requires auth, returns 204 on success, 404 if not found |

The `TaskUpdate.model_dump(exclude_unset=True)` pattern ensures fields not sent in the request body aren't overwritten to `None` — only explicitly provided fields are applied.
